First we have to substitute "weight" by "mass"; "there is no gravity" in
the Air Level according to the Nethack message. With  p = m * v  and the
conservation of momentum  p1 = p2  and  m1 * v1 = m2 * v2  you would get
a higher speed than the thrown object if the mass of the thrown object
is larger than your mass. If you move in vacuum one would move arbitrary
distances either way, throwing objects of more or less mass, just the
velocity of your travel would vary. So with the time discrete simulation
model of Nethack you would indeed travel farther until the monsters turn
will come. The problematic question is the deceleration, that you finally
stop. This might be explanable if the medium you travel through has some
viscosity, then you will be slowed down. I am not quite sure whether you
will be affected by that in a different way if you travel faster; if so
then the Nethack model would be quite a good approximation, IMO.
But I have decades to have heard or read about mechanics so everything I
wrote may be wrong. That's just how I thought the world would work. :-}

